{
  "In the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth.": "e1e1f5e1738c9f78",
  "The earth was formless and empty. Darkness was on the surface of the deep.": "a5afb77eaa1f69ba",
  "God's Spirit was hovering over the surface of the waters.": "39bbeeb9297a5f02",
  "God said, \"Let there be light,\" and there was light.": "6a48a1452f050fb4",
  "God saw the light, and saw that it was good. God divided the light from the darkness.": "3c41138c70070025",
  "God called the light \"day\", and the darkness he called \"night\". There was evening and there was morning, the first day.": "e5114db24116a8e1",
  "God said, \"Let there be an expanse in the middle of the waters, and let it divide the waters from the waters.\"": "b42358ff079b878a",
  "God called the expanse \"sky\". There was evening and there was morning, a second day.": "1ec8c30d4bf04752",
  "God said, \"Let the waters under the sky be gathered together to one place, and let the dry land appear,\" and it was so.": "f153c25b1d18515e",
  "God called the dry land \"earth\", and the gathering of the waters he called \"seas\". God saw that it was good.": "061b603615feb8f7",
  "God said, \"Let the earth yield grass, herbs yielding seeds, and fruit trees bearing fruit.\"": "caf3f4fa035cf66d",
  "There was evening and there was morning, a third day.": "8b620e7860912441",
  "Israel and the Philistines were gathered for battle.": "c49874039dd37cfc",
  "A champion came out from the camp of the Philistines, named Goliath. He was tall and powerful.": "653525de9a584661",
  "Each day Goliath challenged the armies of Israel, shouting, \"Choose a man to fight me!\"": "cc0245aca65b6d7f",
  "When the men of Israel heard him, they were dismayed and greatly afraid.": "ccf855bbf5a59da3",
  "David was the youngest of eight brothers, and he kept his father's sheep.": "24962c474e76705c",
  "His three eldest brothers had followed Saul to the battle.": "6be9cfbc82a46e71",
  "Jesse said to his son David, \"Carry this bread quickly to your brothers at the camp.\"": "8235f7d0fee3501f",
  "When David arrived at the camp, he heard the giant's challenge and saw the men of Israel flee in terror.": "d1c099c3fa6518a5",
  "David asked, \"Who is this man who defies the armies of the living God?\"": "2c2c8f79440e6c13",
  "When King Saul was told what David had said, he sent for him.": "069391f9984b4dae",
  "David said to Saul, \"Let no one's heart fail. Your servant will go and fight this Philistine.\"": "6c9517acb8b3df03",
  "Saul said, \"You can't go to fight him. You are just a boy, and he has been a warrior since his youth.\"": "3e67d0e505f416d7",
  "David replied, \"When a lion took a lamb from the flock, I struck it down and killed it. The Lord who saved me from the lion will save me from this Philistine.\"": "fa270f7ce0a2e6b0",
  "Saul said, \"Go, and may the Lord be with you.\"": "55f9c2930a3e1637",
  "Saul clothed David with his own armor and a bronze helmet, with a sword over the armor.": "e5f81f861076f9b6",
  "David tried to walk, but he could not, for he had not tested it.": "09f6ae393370ca59",
  "David took it all off and went as he was — a shepherd boy with his staff.": "ff8ce71edd7362d9",
  "He chose five smooth stones from the brook.": "19e7719bdb53fc9f",
  "He put them in his shepherd's bag, and with his sling in his hand, he drew near to the Philistine.": "82b32e51a66ea032",
  "When the Philistine looked and saw David, he was angry, for David was just a young boy.": "5d7a8ed1a92e3435",
  "The Philistine said, \"Am I a dog, that you come at me with sticks?\"": "b118f110a1159a40",
  "David replied, \"You come with a sword and a spear. I come in the name of the Lord, the God of the armies of Israel.\"": "66d069ed163c05cb",
  "\"This day all the earth shall know that there is a God in Israel.\"": "17d35efb79a25d27",
  "As the Philistine arose to meet him, David ran quickly toward the battle line.": "8a00f6078d558697",
  "He put his hand in his bag, took out a stone, and placed it in his sling.": "1db7232aebbb0cb5",
  "He slung the stone, and it flew through the air.": "ce631c698b194df4",
  "The stone struck the Philistine's forehead, and he fell face down on the ground.": "de0ea5850ecea10e",
  "David defeated the giant. The army of Israel rose up and shouted in triumph.": "f70404936a988301",
  "Many years passed, and the wickedness of mankind grew great upon the earth.": "7d1b451ca508e046",
  "People were cruel and violent, and they had forgotten the God who made them.": "d249971363dbfca4",
  "It grieved God's heart to see what the world had become.": "69a92c195a475fa2",
  "But there was one man, named Noah, who walked with God and found favor in his eyes.": "fc91fc1306558877",
  "Noah was a righteous man, blameless among the people of his time.": "e2d3bc765d49edff",
  "Noah had three sons: Shem, Ham, and Japheth.": "10e01182c45beeb2",
  "God said to Noah, \"I am going to bring a great flood upon the earth.\"": "a852314b1a583f75",
  "\"Make yourself an ark of cypress wood, sealed inside and out.\"": "c35ab86cd27f7590",
  "\"Make it long and tall, with rooms inside and a roof above.\"": "b9661d43c47a7140",
  "\"You and your wife, your sons and their wives will go in, with two of every kind of animal.\"": "0b5c2465749a8722",
  "So Noah and his sons began to build. The work took many years.": "ec2f6558e10b87ed",
  "Noah did everything just as God had commanded him.": "75e95622096aa27a",
  "Many years later, the ark was completed.": "e0b87e130ed24d7c",
  "God said to Noah, \"Enter the ark, you and all your household.\"": "40da2bcb79f8055d",
  "The animals came to the ark in pairs, male and female.": "44803c3d30b3724b",
  "Beasts of every kind, birds of every kind, and creatures that crawl on the ground.": "9dfbb6f3c7b2bcaa",
  "Noah and his wife, his three sons, and their wives entered the ark.": "81c02b5351f4b190",
  "Then the Lord closed the door behind them.": "69cbc2a2e4d06b97",
  "Soon, the rain began to pour down from the sky.": "f35472557a4b9a5f",
  "The rain continued for forty days and forty nights without stopping.": "d9b4c6e72cb0c854",
  "The waters increased and rose higher and higher upon the earth.": "1f5a6e4641519354",
  "It covered the trees, the hills, and even the highest mountains.": "2bcb5daac7303cb0",
  "But the ark was lifted up and floated safely above the waters.": "6ef99e8d32743c45",
  "Inside the ark, Noah, his family, and every animal were kept safe.": "d47147d0b985a226",
  "After many days, the rain ceased to fall.": "4739d0cac1b07ebc",
  "God sent a wind across the earth, and the waters began to recede.": "c93c773616cb64bb",
  "The ark came to rest on the mountains of Ararat.": "69dd55336cf6b3b8",
  "Noah opened the window of the ark that he had made.": "1a3e3e17b2198981",
  "He sent out a dove to see whether the waters had gone down.": "e9d511eacf5da30d",
  "The dove returned because it found no place to rest.": "cb535f4dc0cb4ee9",
  "Seven days later, Noah sent the dove out once more.": "75039ddca8c59b18",
  "This time, the dove returned with a fresh olive leaf in its beak.": "5c3f92f582b1f704",
  "God said to Noah, \"Leave the ark, you and all who are with you.\"": "646649a99ac292c0",
  "Then God set a rainbow in the clouds as a sign of his promise.": "79dbf00aa348db24",
  "\"This is my covenant: never again will a flood destroy all life on earth.\"": "0d3431c4969d0443",
  "Whenever the rainbow appears, it reminds us of the covenant between God and the earth.": "ad3d493b3a49d192",
  "In ancient times, there lived a prophet named Jonah.": "4f7c2bcd10121041",
  "The Lord said to Jonah, \"Arise, go to the great city of Nineveh.\"": "56b26030aff57985",
  "\"Cry out against it, for their wickedness has come up before me.\"": "91794c0daec0937e",
  "But Jonah refused, and tried to flee from the presence of the Lord.": "a84f90abb63f3334",
  "He went down to the harbor and boarded a ship sailing in the opposite direction.": "04e6c6ac88012efc",
  "While Jonah slept below deck, a mighty storm arose on the sea.": "39cfe29ed16241eb",
  "The wind howled and the waves crashed against the ship.": "35b264c05141ee3d",
  "The sailors were terrified, thinking the ship would be torn apart.": "b00991a3648841f3",
  "They awakened Jonah and demanded, \"What have you done?\"": "bfe0ceb5a3c58240",
  "Jonah said, \"I am fleeing from the Lord. Throw me into the sea, and it will calm down.\"": "8ceefd7097e1ab31",
  "They threw Jonah into the sea, and at once, the raging storm grew calm.": "743768b19e2f687e",
  "But the Lord prepared a great fish to swallow Jonah and protect him.": "178202abacabd18f",
  "Jonah remained in the belly of the great fish for three days and three nights.": "b333ebfe8a3d46c0",
  "From inside the fish, Jonah cried out to the Lord his God.": "ed11f71ee1e5b276",
  "\"In my distress I called to the Lord, and he answered me.\"": "c72b22701297c0d9",
  "\"I will keep my promise to you, O Lord.\"": "c35ec0a3e569cc7a",
  "Then the Lord commanded the fish, and it spit Jonah out onto the dry land.": "a5f59538534a5600",
  "A second time, the Lord said to Jonah, \"Arise, go to Nineveh, that great city.\"": "8ac2921363fd856c",
  "This time, Jonah obeyed and went to Nineveh.": "b6580e8153bd5120",
  "He proclaimed throughout the city, \"In forty days, Nineveh will be overthrown!\"": "ed975ac34d5bebce",
  "The people of Nineveh believed Jonah's message and trembled.": "bc4041b83e4d985e",
  "Even the king rose from his throne and humbled himself.": "2eaa31d59c7ca2cc",
  "Everyone repented and turned away from their evil ways.": "7400e224f2f535b9",
  "When God saw what they had done, he relented and spared the city.": "ccad67f2610029e1",
  "But Jonah was deeply displeased and became furious.": "9a168a3e45d75a7d",
  "He prayed, \"Lord, why did you show mercy to these people?\"": "1af518df706bb45b",
  "\"I knew you were merciful, and that is why I tried to flee.\"": "2b8cc8cef05b32ac",
  "Jonah left the city, sat east of it, and waited to see what would happen.": "b4097255c98c607c",
  "The sun was burning, and Jonah grew weary.": "6c9e01df0287f82a",
  "The Lord caused a leafy vine to grow over Jonah, providing shade above his head.": "3f12d2c03a57b777",
  "Jonah was overjoyed by the cool shade of the vine.": "4479c98ef545cf53",
  "But the next morning, a worm attacked the vine and it withered.": "ca5ef49ae632b364",
  "A scorching east wind blew, and Jonah grew faint under the burning sun.": "090456026ad5dca5",
  "Jonah said, \"It would be better for me to die than to keep living.\"": "d7204d6ca3cce174",
  "God said, \"You care about a vine that you did not plant or tend, that grew in a night and perished in a night.\"": "85896a6ce84b0a00",
  "\"Should I not have compassion on the great city of Nineveh, with so many people in it?\"": "ce6d06de00fed881",
  "Daniel was a man of excellent spirit who served the king with wisdom.": "b0cc205b6212eead",
  "The king favored Daniel above all the others.": "ae395f585b2661b2",
  "The king planned to set Daniel over the entire kingdom.": "6c311dc6b8e8a05f",
  "But the other officials grew envious of Daniel.": "9c7f841c647edb87",
  "They schemed, \"How can we find a charge against Daniel?\"": "1454fbc5d2891218",
  "They knew that Daniel prayed three times a day, every day.": "5383421a59a78126",
  "So they devised a plan and approached the king.": "6ddfc697f4afaf53",
  "\"O great king, issue a new decree!\" they declared.": "0de47513b008a132",
  "\"For thirty days, no person shall offer prayer to any god or man except you.\"": "d579bae160ff99e6",
  "\"Whoever breaks this decree shall be cast into the den of lions.\"": "3f92c78ea5afd7a8",
  "The king signed the decree, making it official.": "fb9242ca699fe49f",
  "When Daniel heard about the decree, he went home, opened his window toward Jerusalem, and prayed as he always did.": "de19b3c7f67707f9",
  "The officials caught Daniel in prayer and rushed to inform the king.": "16d776ded2d42b1c",
  "\"Daniel continues to pray to his God three times a day, ignoring your decree!\" they reported.": "bcbba7951497a7b4",
  "The king was deeply troubled, for he cared about Daniel.": "3b36c41cd21b7bde",
  "Until sunset, the king sought a way to rescue Daniel, but the decree could not be reversed.": "47c0f8959a13a60d",
  "Finally, the king commanded that Daniel be cast into the den of lions.": "d53858284e3e6ea5",
  "The king said to Daniel, \"May your God, whom you serve continually, deliver you.\"": "570648ddd2e60c9d",
  "A massive stone was rolled over the entrance of the den and sealed.": "dcabb034d5b516c6",
  "That night, the king refused all food and could not sleep.": "9d5cf589b42999f8",
  "At the break of dawn, the king hurried to the den.": "e36ca69a2857a157",
  "\"Daniel, servant of the living God, has your God been able to deliver you from the lions?\"": "36922abd668d11a4",
  "Daniel replied, \"My God sent his angel and shut the mouths of the lions. They have not harmed me.\"": "e719fd1e4ddfb0eb",
  "Overjoyed, the king proclaimed throughout his kingdom, \"The God of Daniel is mighty and everlasting!\"": "0927a2f98cd472ef"
}
